			<div class="content" id="post-content-4840813">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A skull that is sapient that can make sound anywhere in the world as well as hear everything that is being done in the world. The skull can also make exact imitations of sound and voices. The skull also knows languages that were wiped out and some that aren't even recorded in history. The skull can move its lower jaw but doesn't need it to make sound. The pitch of the sound made from the skull seems to be limitless.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The skull was obtained from a cult that was taking skulls from people. It was sent when a police officer that was actually a foundation personnel was asked by the skull for help. On the way to a site the skull conducted a interview with a researcher at the site. Through the interviews it is revealed that the it became this because it saw something it shouldn't. The skull suffers a tremendous amount of mental damage as it can hear all of the suffering of the world. Singing in cafeteria however has been an emotional anchor an idea thought by the foundation to relieve it of some pain. This has worked even though only a little. The skull is going through therapy every week.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The hook is show readers a fairly simple idea but the more you read into the story you realise the skull has a very mysterious and sad past through the interviews conducted during therapy sessions.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> This was inspired by SCP-774 as a skull that made sound. I then added hear no evil, speak no evil, see no evil concept and worked the skull's backstory around that. This my first time writing an scp so any feedback is appreciated. Also if anything isn't clear please let me know</p>

